This Splunk Enterprise query searches Sysmon process creation logs and extracts the executable name (`Image`) and full command line (`CommandLine`) from the raw XML event data. 
It then filters for suspicious activity involving PowerShell or scheduled task creation (`schtasks`) and displays the timestamp, process name, and executed command in a readable table format.


index=main sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "Name=[\"']Image[\"']>(?<Image>[^<]+)"
| rex field=_raw "Name=[\"']CommandLine[\"']>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)"
| search Image="*powershell.exe"
| table _time Image CommandLine

index=main sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)"
| rex field=_raw "Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)"
| search Image="*powershell*" OR CommandLine="*schtasks*"
| table _time Image CommandLine
